      translit: "Innā lillāhi wa innā ilayhi rāji'ūn.",
      meaning: "Indeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we return.",
      gloss: "Surah Al-Baqarah 2:156. The verse you say when you hear of a death. We had said it about other people for decades before we had to say it about her. I have said it every day since.",
